'''bellicosely''' (bel′i-kōs-li), ''adv.'' In a bellicose or warlike manner; pugnaciously.
{{smaller block|Anything like rallying the more ''bellicosely'' inclined of the pilgrims would, under the circumstances, be out of the question. {{right|''O’Donovan'', Merv, x.}}}}

'''bellicous†''' (bel′i-kus), ''a.'' [As ''bellicose'', < L. ''bellicosus''; or < L. ''bellicus'': see ''bellicose'', ''bellic.''] Bellicose: as, “''bellicous'' nations,” ''Sir T. Smith'', Commonwealth of Eng.

